# The build context deliberately *includes* .git: `go build` reads the VCS revision from it
# and stamps it into the binary, which is what /meta reports and what makes a run
# certifiable (ag-sept-plan-new.md §6.4). An image built without it serves an unstamped
# binary and every run against it is uncertifiable — the failure looks like a harness bug.
bin/
docs/
test/
deploy/observability/grafana/
*.md
.github/
